A||||4||Austin||Changing ribbed moldings to rounded ones.||||4||
Z||000000||Austin||10-13-2001||01:04 AM||||Greetings. <P>I want to change my ribbed moldings to rounded ones.  Is such a thing possible.  I believe it is but must seek the great wisdom of the Fiero people first.  So, is it possible to change my ribbed moldings to rounded ones?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-13-2001||07:33 AM||||The rounded moldings on the GT's rear fascia are a painted part of the fascia and not a separate molding piece.  Also on the GT, the small front dart molding on the front fascia side is bolted on and you need to remove the front nose, or maybe the wheel well to access the nuts holding the part on.  I imagine the ribbed molding is held on the same way.  I believe the remaining molding pieces can be replaced, by accessing the clips holding molding on from inside the door panels and quarter panels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||10-13-2001||07:49 AM||||Also on the early coupes, the molding between the front wheel well and the marker light is molded into the front fascia(not removeable.)  This area is part of the removeable marker light on my 88 GT, I'm not sure about the other aero noses.<p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||10-13-2001||08:04 AM||||There is a difference in the ribbed and round molded front aero fascia other than the replaceable bullet piece, as I recently found out.<BR> It can be altered fairly easily however.<BR>Note photos below.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Molded.JPG"> <BR>The boxed portion of the ribbed molding is molded into the front fascia. It can be cut away and a supporting piece of the same material attached to the rear with the proper repair adhesive.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nomold.JPG"> <BR>The 86-88 GT front aero fascia has the molding as part of the running light.<BR>Coy <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tina||10-13-2001||10:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Austin:<BR><B> So, is it possible to change my ribbed moldings to rounded ones?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I know it works the other way around.<BR>(Rounded to ribbed)<BR>Did have to change the front and rear end as well though.<BR>(molding is non removable on these panels)<BR>And yes, Wolfhound is right.<BR>Some slight differences, but workable.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
